%% plays.glp --- the DGC mini-app activated as the super-app activates it (GSG paper, Section 2, "Activation and joining"): by run/3, under the type identity of its entry miniapp/3, with its grants; and, for the two executions that transact, with the two ends of one root channel handed to them as their conversation, the play standing in for the social graph, as ../gb/plays.glp does.  The persons are scripted (person.glp), each under its role, and the play returns their screens.  DGC requires the day for Issue denominated bond (DGC:1: today(Alice,Today), gt(Day,Today)), which the compiled agent reads from the machine's clock by now/1, in whole days, floor(T / 86400000), UTC (vGLP, Section 5.4, "Speech-act schemas as local specifications"); the play runs on one machine, which has one clock, and the scripted persons set it to day 1 by their steps clock(T) (person.glp).  A run does not end --- the agent's request question stays open and the person channel never closes --- so once each agent has taken its own transactions until none holds and no trigger is left, the run suspends, and a play's result is read off a partial stream.

imported procedure person#miniapp_person(Key?, Constant?, List(Key)?, Channel(PersonOut(Drawn), PersonIn(Drawn))?, Stream(Seen)).

%% play_denominated(A, B): alice and bob, one conversation, the denomination usd.  Each establishes their identity (GKK:1); they come to know each other (GKK:2, an act of both); each issues two usd-denominated coins of their own, and alice three usd-denominated Alice-bonds due day 10, later than day 1, the current date (DGC:1, Issue denominated bond); alice swaps her two Alice-coins for bob's two Bob-coins, of the one denomination, and he answers yes (DGC:2, Swap); bob accepts one more usd-denominated Alice-coin in payment (DGC:3, Accept) and pays alice one of her own Alice-coins (Coins:1, Pay issuer); and alice pays it to bob, who accepts it (DGC:4, Pay own accepted coins), his acceptance used up.
exported procedure play_denominated(Stream(Seen), Stream(Seen)).
play_denominated(A?, B?) :-
    self_module(M),
    find_type(miniapp/3, T),
    run(miniapp(alice, ch(GA?, DA), ch([conversation(bob, ch(BA?, AB))], _)), T?, M?),
    person # miniapp_person(alice, alice, [bob], ch(DA?, GA), A),
    run(miniapp(bob, ch(GB?, DB), ch([conversation(alice, ch(AB?, BA))], _)), T?, M?),
    person # miniapp_person(bob, bob, [alice], ch(DB?, GB), B).

%% play_mint(A): alice alone, under the role mint (person.glp), with no conversation: the mini-app activated by run/3 with an empty stream of conversations, as the super-app activates it with no invitation (GSG paper, Section 2, "Activation and joining"; ../dgc_mint_boot.glp).  She sets the clock to day 1, establishes her identity (GKK:1) and issues three usd-denominated coins of her own (First issue).
exported procedure play_mint(Stream(Seen)).
play_mint(A?) :-
    self_module(M),
    find_type(miniapp/3, T),
    run(miniapp(alice, ch(GA?, DA), ch([], _)), T?, M?),
    person # miniapp_person(alice, mint, [], ch(DA?, GA), A).
